{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792234400,"nonce":"ldxhchKUEN6DL9hYN0lB7I2kAV8=","title":"The wasm runtime object defines no libm: a side module that does float math is refused at link","message":"Reported by ashui-f2 (ashui git-bug 0c8c9a0). A Rust side module built for wasm32-wasip1-threads (blinc_abi.wasm, same recipe as hlwgpu's xgpu.wasm) imports acos acosf atan2 atan2f cos cosf exp2f hypotf log2 log2f pow powf sin sinf tan tanf from env. `ash --build smoke.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1-threads smoke.hl` with it beside the output lowers every function and then refuses: 'a native library beside the output imports 10 function(s) this runtime does not define, the first few being acosf, atan2f, cosf, exp2f, hypotf, log2, log2f, powf'.\n\nwasi-libc keeps libm in libc.a, and scripts/build_wasm_runtime.py links only the members named in LIBRARY_LIBC. Fix: add the libm set to that list (every name checked against libc.a's symbol table); unused members are tree-shaken from a module.","files":null}]}